      <MissionDesc>The Interfaith Shelter Network of San Diego (the Organization) is a non-profit, public benefit corporation, incorporated on August 1, 2010 (formerly Ecumenical Council of San Diego County, incorporated April 24, 1970), under the laws of the state of California, to work collaboratively, through its Rotational Shelter Program, with local human service agencies, local governments and local congregations to provide winter shelters and other services and resources to homeless individuals and families at congregational shelter sites throughout the San Diego region.</MissionDesc>
